const password = process.env.MONGODB_PASSWORD;. this doesnt link back to the password. what exactly do i need to do to make this defined instead of undefined

process.env.MONGODB_PASSWORD doesn't automatically "link" to anything. It only has a value if you've defined an environment variable named MONGODB_PASSWORD.

Option 1 (recommended): Use a single MONGODB_URI

This is the simplest approach.

In Render, create an environment variable:

Key: MONGODB_URI
Value: mongodb+srv://username:password@cluster0.rnhnurl.mongodb.net/?retryWrites=true&w=majority&appName=Cluster0

Then in your code:

const { MongoClient } = require("mongodb");

const client = new MongoClient(process.env.MONGODB_URI);

No need for a separate MONGODB_PASSWORD variable.

Option 2: Store the password separately

If you want to build the URI in code, then you must define the password in Render.

In Render → Environment, add:

Key: MONGODB_PASSWORD
Value: yourActualPassword

Then this works:

const password = encodeURIComponent(process.env.MONGODB_PASSWORD);

const uri = `mongodb+srv://li.huybrecht%40ehb.be:${password}@cluster0.rnhnurl.mongodb.net/?retryWrites=true&w=majority&appName=Cluster0`;

const client = new MongoClient(uri);

If process.env.MONGODB_PASSWORD is undefined, it means Render doesn't have an environment variable with that exact name.

How to check

Add:

console.log(process.env.MONGODB_PASSWORD);

If it prints:

undefined

then the environment variable is missing or has a different name.

