The important line is:

Pinged your deployment. You successfully connected to MongoDB!

That means your MongoDB connection is working.

The problem is this:

==> Application exited early

On Render, a web service must keep running by listening on a port. If your program connects to MongoDB, prints a message, and then finishes, Render considers it crashed because there's no server process left running.

Check whether you're starting your server

You should have something like:

const express = require("express");
const app = express();

const PORT = process.env.PORT || 3000;

app.listen(PORT, () => {
console.log(`Server listening on port ${PORT}`);
});

If you're missing app.listen(...), your application will exit after it finishes executing.

If you're not building a web server

If your application is just a script (for example, it imports data into MongoDB and exits), then it shouldn't be deployed as a Render Web Service. Instead, you should use:

a Background Worker, or
a Cron Job, depending on what the script does.
